---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import P from "../components/P.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import reads from "../data/reads.json";
const M = ["Morabito Salvatore 4","Morabito Sebastiana 14","Messina Salvatore 16","Monforte Salvatore 39",
  "Masano Giuseppa 18","Molino Domenica 56","Malfitana Giovanna 61","Masano Rosaria 67",
  "Musumeci Rosaria 80","Masano Grazia 89","Musumeci Maria 107","Musumeci Salvatore 112",
  "Moschella Carmela 113","Musumeci Venera 133","Monti Salvatore 153","Mangano Rosa 159",
  "Mazza Rosaria 167","Messina Giovanni 180","Musumeci Giuseppa 190","Messina Francesco 124",
  "Mangeri Salvatore 199","Masano Sebastiano 201","Mazza Venerio 205"];
---
<Base title="Piedimonte Etneo, Births 1879" eyebrow="The register read, 10 September 2026"
      dek="The volume that should hold Salvatore Mazza's birth. It does not.">

  <section class="blk">
    <p class="lede">The family tree says <strong>Salvatore Mazza was born at Piedimonte Etneo in
    1879</strong>. He is the grandfather of <P n="Sebastiano Mazza" />, the second generation of the
    surname line, and his act of birth would name his father <P n="Rosario Mazza" /> with an age and
    a trade — which is the one document that could join the
    <a href={u("/mazza")}>hundred and ten unattached Mazza</a> to this family.</p>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:1rem">The volume exists, it is digitised, and it has now been
    read. <strong>He is not in it.</strong></p>
  </section>

  <section class="blk">
    <h2>The volume</h2>
    <div class="rec" style="margin-top:16px">
      <div class="k">Archive</div><div class="v">Archivio di Stato di Catania</div><div class="w"></div>
      <div class="k">Series</div><div class="v">Stato civile italiano › Piedimonte Etneo › Nati</div><div class="w">1879</div>
      <div class="k">Shelf-mark</div><div class="v">segnatura 8956</div><div class="w"></div>
      <div class="k">Ark</div><div class="v"><a href="https://antenati.cultura.gov.it/ark:/12657/an_ua83492" rel="noopener">an_ua83492 ↗</a></div><div class="w">81 images</div>
      <div class="k">Supplement</div><div class="v"><a href="https://antenati.cultura.gov.it/ark:/12657/an_ua83493" rel="noopener">an_ua83493 ↗</a> — segnatura 8957, suppl. 2</div><div class="w">not yet read</div>
      <div class="k">Index</div><div class="v">Indice annuale, alphabetical, pages 72–73 (images 79–80)</div><div class="w"></div>
    </div>
    <p class="cap">Two acts to an image, act 126 on image 54 and act 167 on image 74 — which is how
    the index entry was turned into a page number without reading the book.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="blk">
    <div class="lab">The finding</div>
    <h2 style="margin-top:.4rem">Two Mazza births in 1879, and neither is Salvatore</h2>
    <p class="dek" style="margin:.9rem 0 1.2rem">The annual index covers the whole year for the
    comune. Under <strong>M</strong> it carries twenty-three entries, and exactly two of them are
    Mazza:</p>
    <div class="evlist" style="margin-bottom:20px">
      {M.map((s) => {
        const n = s.split(" ").pop(), nm = s.slice(0, -n.length - 1);
        const isMazza = nm.startsWith("Mazza");
        return <div><b>{n}</b>{isMazza ? <strong style="color:var(--terra)">{nm}</strong> : nm}</div>;
      })}
    </div>
    <figure style="margin:0">
      <img src={u("/plates/pe-1879-index-M.jpg")} alt="The M section of the 1879 annual index"
           style="border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:3px;max-width:520px;width:100%" />
      <figcaption class="cap">Piedimonte Etneo, Nati 1879, Indice annuale, page 72 — Archivio di
      Stato di Catania (Antenati an_ua83492, image 79).</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="blk">
    <div class="lab">Act 167</div>
    <h2 style="margin-top:.4rem">Rosaria Mazza, 28 October 1879</h2>
    <div class="hero-plate" style="margin-top:1.2rem">
      <img src={u("/plates/act167-mazza-rosaria.jpg")} alt="Piedimonte Etneo birth register 1879, act 167" />
      <div>
        <blockquote style="margin:0 0 .9rem">L'anno milleottocentosettanta<strong>nove</strong>, addì
        <strong>ventinove</strong> di <strong>Ottobre</strong>… è comparso <strong>Mazza Pasquale</strong>,
        di anni <strong>cinquanta</strong>, <strong>bracciante</strong>, domiciliato in Piedimonte
        Etneo… nella casa posta in <strong>Via Terremorte</strong>… da <strong>Greco Concetta,
        industriosa, sua moglie, seco lui convivente</strong>… è nato un bambino di sesso femminino…
        a cui dà il nome di <strong>Rosaria</strong>.</blockquote>
        <p>A second Mazza household at Piedimonte Etneo, and a complete one: <strong>Pasquale Mazza</strong>,
        born about <strong>1829</strong>, a day-labourer, living on <strong>Via Terremorte</strong>
        with his wife <strong>Concetta Greco</strong>. Their daughter was born at half past six on the
        morning of the 28th and registered the next morning at twenty-five past nine.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:.8rem">A note added in the margin twenty-four years later records that
        she <strong>married Giuseppe Monforte, son of the late Salvatore, on 26 April 1903</strong>.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:.8rem"><strong>He is not Rosario.</strong> This household does not join
        the line — but it is a documented Mazza family of the right town in the right decade, and it
        is the first Italian record this archive has read for any of them.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="blk" style="border-bottom:0">
    <h2>What it means</h2>
    <div class="prose" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <p>The tree's claim that Salvatore Mazza was born at Piedimonte Etneo in 1879 is now
      <strong>disputed</strong> — asserted in the family record and not supported by the register that
      should contain it. Three things could be true:</p>
      <ul style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:14px;line-height:1.75;color:var(--ink-2);padding-left:20px">
        <li><strong>The year is wrong.</strong> Most likely. 1879 in the tree carries no source, and a
        year either side has not been checked. The volumes for 1875–1885 are all digitised.</li>
        <li><strong>The town is wrong.</strong> Salvatore died at <em>Catania</em> in 1929, and the
        family also appears at <strong>Mascali</strong> and <strong>Giarre</strong>, both within a few
        kilometres.</li>
        <li><strong>He is in the supplement.</strong> Act 205 — <strong>Mazza Venerio</strong> — sits
        in the second volume, which has not been read. <em>Venerio</em> is not <em>Salvatore</em>, but
        the supplement holds the late and irregular registrations and deserves reading in full.</li>
      </ul>
      <p style="margin-top:14px">Until one of those is settled, the head of the Mazza line stays where
      it is: a man called Rosario about whom one fact is known.
      <a href={u("/open-questions")}>The queue →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
